// ParseBatchForInserts runs the generated parse on the producer and streams
// ready proto-ring slots to the consumer. A bounded batch pool prevents the
// producer from outrunning the consumer while allowing the two stages to
// overlap.
//
// Parsing (JSONL decode + ABI decode) is pure CPU and the producer's
// throughput ceiling on backfill-sized pages, so pages worth the overhead are
// split into line-aligned chunks (splitJSONLChunks) and parsed concurrently
// across parseWorkers() goroutines — each chunk goroutine borrows its own
// ProtoRingBuffer/InsertBatches from a shared pool for the duration of its own
// parse, so no two goroutines mutate the same ring at once. Every chunk's
// parsed blocks are collected, then replayed into onParsed strictly in chunk
// order (ascending block number) once all chunks finish: the eventCount/flush
// contract this returns is unchanged from the single-goroutine path, so the
// ingestion producer loop (which expects onParsed in order, and one flush per
// call) needs no changes. Small pages fall back to a single chunk, which takes
// the original single-goroutine path.
//
// Ring lifetime — PARTIAL fix, path still unsafe at production consumer lag:
// a borrowed ring is released back to the pool only after every block that
// references its *ProtoEventBlock slots has cleared onParsed (see
// putPooledRing calls below), not in a batch immediately after wg.Wait(). This
// closes the WITHIN-one-call race across this page's own chunks. It does NOT
// close the CROSS-page race: putPooledRing's Reset() means the very next
// ParseBatchForInserts call (the next page, same producer goroutine) can
// re-draw this exact ring and overwrite its slots the moment this call
// returns — regardless of whether the consumer, on its own separate
// goroutine, has actually read this page's blocks out of the replay buffer
// yet. onParsed only proves a block reached the replay buffer, not that it
// was consumed. The replayBufCap backpressure gate bounds aggregate backlog
// across ALL pages/rings combined; it does not bound how soon a SPECIFIC
// ring gets recycled, so it does not make this safe. Proven still-corrupting
// at production lag by
// examples/polymarket/generated/parse_batch_coupling_test.go's
// TestParallelPathProtoLifetimeDefect (38996/40000 slots recycled before
// consumption) — see AUDIT.md for the full analysis and real fix options.
// Do not enable this path (SQD_PARSE_WORKERS>1) in production until that
// defect is fixed; Makefile's POLYMARKET_PARSE_WORKERS defaults to 1 to keep
// production on the proven-safe parseBatchForInsertsOne path.
